{
  "title": "Congenital Clasped Thumb",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6085/congenital-clasped-thumb",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 22 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Congenital Clasped Thumb is a congenital pediatric condition that results in a flexion-adduction deformity of the thumb that persists beyond the 3rd or 4th month of life.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with the presence of a flexion-adduction deformity of the thumb, that is often bilateral.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually a trial of nonoperative management with serial splinting and stretching for 3-6 months. Surgical management is indicated for persistent deformity, significant soft tissue defects or, MCP contractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "male-to-female ratio is approx 2.5:1",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "exact causative factors are not well known",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**possible pre-disposing factors** include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "consanguinity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "family history",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "genetics",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "autosomal dominance inheritance of variable expressivity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may be **sporadic**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**attenuation or deficiency of EPB (more common, in mild cases) or EPL, or both**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "associated with 1st web contracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "contracture of adductor pollicis or first dorsal interosseous muscle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "global instability of first MP joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "abnormal articular cartilage of first MP joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Orthopedic considerations",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common manifestations associated with disease",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lower limb anomalies",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "congenital vertical talus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "congenital talipes equinovarus (bilateral)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "upper limb anomalies",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "flexion deformities of the four fingers",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**arthrogryphosis** (congenital joint contractures affect two or more areas in the body)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "digitotalar dysmorphisms",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Freeman-Sheldon syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "X-linked MASA syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
              "header": true,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 3,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Tsuyuguchi Classification of Clasped Thumb**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type I (Supple clasped thumb)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Thumb can be passively abducted and extended against resistance of thumb flexors. No other digital anomaly present.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6085/images/tileshop.fcgi-3..jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type II (Clasped thumb with contracture)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Thumb cannot be passively extended and abducted. This may occur with or without other digital anomalies.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6085/images/tileshop.fcgi-3..jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type III (Rigid clasped thumb)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Clasped thumb that is associated with **arthrogryposis** and marked soft-tissue deficits.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6085/images/tileshop.fcgi-3..jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "persistent flexion-adduction deformity beyond 3rd or 4th month of life, usually bilateral",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "family history",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pre-natal history",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain usually with a contracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "associated with other musculo-skeletal deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Examination",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "type of clasped thumb",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "associated anomalies",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "serial splinting and stretching for 3-6 months",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**first-line treatment for all types**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "begin treatment around the age of 6 month old",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcome",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "good definitive results with Type I congenital deformities when one of the EPL or EPB tendons are present",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "poor results with Type I deformities when both EPL/EPB tendons are absent",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "poor results with Type II or III deformities",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "EIP tendon transfer to EPL",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Type I or II** with residual deficiency in active extension",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "thumb reconstruction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "failed conservative treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "soft-tissue deficiency in the thumb-index finger webspace (Type III)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**Type II or III deformity** with significant MCP joint contractures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "arthrodesis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "severe deformities when skin release and tendon transfer cannot overcome joint deformity.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Thumb reconstruction**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "delayed until the age of **3 to 5 years old**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "procedure based on amount of contracture and may include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "1st web widening",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "transposition flap of skin (dorsal rotational advancement flap)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "four-flap or five-flap Z plasty",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "deepening the first webspace by releasing soft-tissue",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "releasing origins of thenar musculature from transverse carpal ligament",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "releasing joint capsule of first MP joint",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "tendon transfer",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "FPL Z-lengthening in the forearm",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "EPB and EPL absence is best reconstructed with tendon transfer",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "isolated EPB absence will not usually require tendon transfer",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Cosmetic appearance**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Instability of the MP joint**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Reduced thumb function**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
